#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:5
#: b25c3c428d3f40358c99bd254e381e0b
msgid "Limiting Maximum Battery Power Draw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:7
#: cf73715fd7bb497d93ecbf68fac3a615
msgid "Sometimes power needs to be limited to prevent issues with battery sag or overheating. This can occur because of the use of lower C rated batteries, high power motors, high ambient temperatures, uncooled engines or ESCs, or other reasons. This topic discusses ways to limit the maximum power draw from batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:10
#: 6d524a366a554f23ac1ecbb269f8ede9
msgid "Methods to Limit Maximum Power Draw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:12
#: c3be4f688a7044989ef54721e9d5efc1
msgid "The first and simplest is to restrict :ref:`MOT_THR_MAX<MOT_THR_MAX>` to a lower value. This limits the maximum throttle controlled allowed. Unfortunately, this will not set an exact power limit and might require some trial and error to find the right setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:14
#: 412d2708440f4c56b80e4d7828b906e6
msgid "A better way is to use a power limiting parameter (shown for first battery monitor):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:16
#: 35cc898c54eb4d7788299dddbef2ae94
msgid ":ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:18
#: 49388641c91948d19d4b92d88f6cb854
msgid "The :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>` parameter can be used to limit the total wattage that can be drawn from the battery(s). If battery power exceeds this value then the system will reduce max throttle (:ref:`MOT_THR_MAX<MOT_THR_MAX>`) to lower the power draw. If power demand is reduced, the max throttle will slowly grow back to :ref:`MOT_THR_MAX<MOT_THR_MAX>`. Use 0 (default) to disable this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:20
#: 71e370ae2e5c4ccab0e336245b0bc01f
msgid "The power limiting feature uses a low-pass filter to smooth out the power readings and prevent rapid fluctuations in throttle. In some cases this can lead to a delay in power limiter activating or deactivating. The :ref:`MOT_BAT_WATT_TC <MOT_BAT_WATT_TC>` parameter can be adjusted to change the time constant of this filter and improve the responsiveness of the power limiter. The default value is 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:22
#: 657aca37cb854d3fb8958c5c2ef72e4b
msgid "The following table shows the effect of different :ref:`MOT_BAT_WATT_TC <MOT_BAT_WATT_TC>` values on the responsiveness of the power limiter. The power ratio is the ratio of actual power draw to the :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>` limit. The percentage values show how much the max throttle is reduced per second at different power ratios for different time constants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:25
#: 5a28d8bf7118423cbb79e99e0c1a718a
msgid "Power Ratio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:25
#: a204e42fa32f49f5971925b1ce8cdda0
msgid "``MOT_BAT_WATT_TC=1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:25
#: 3f16ab9a99df4a8d8923f2270b5a1a6b
msgid "``MOT_BAT_WATT_TC=2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:25
#: 61c83f234c9249f48e0e9a05b1540553
msgid "``MOT_BAT_WATT_TC=5``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:27
#: 4fe42836069b4c86860c5bb82265a1a0
msgid "1.1 1.5 2 5 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:27
#: c1320806cee846df8cf3cf6ec6041bf1
msgid "reduced 9%/sec reduced 49%/sec reduced 98%/sec reduced 392%/sec reduced 882%/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:27
#: db8c2b1300564253a34ad035ade850fb
msgid "reduced 4%/sec reduced 24%/sec reduced 49%/sec reduced 198%/sec reduced 445%/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:27
#: 77e3349b96054ea995016cc883e941fe
msgid "reduced 1%/sec reduced 9%/sec reduced 19%/sec reduced 79%/sec reduced 179%/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/batt-watt-max.rst:34
#: 6d83f6380aa3481fb59c1f98946fa970
msgid "For example, if the power draw is 50% above the :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>` limit (power ratio of 1.5) and :ref:`MOT_BAT_WATT_TC <MOT_BAT_WATT_TC>` is set to 2, then the max throttle will be reduced by 24% per second. If the power draw is 10 times above the limit (power ratio of 10) and :ref:`MOT_BAT_WATT_TC <MOT_BAT_WATT_TC>` is set to 5, then the max throttle will be reduced by 179% per second."
msgstr ""
